 ## Capture
 
-A confirmed pantry order is captured for its authorized amount: `larder/capture.py` calls the card gateway and
-returns its charge id.
+A confirmed pantry order is captured for its authorized amount:
+[the capture implementation](../../larder/capture.py) calls the card gateway and returns its charge id.
 
 ## Retries
 
-A capture that times out is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all, one after the other.
+A capture that times out is tried again, up to 5 attempts in all, with pauses of 2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds before
+successive retries. These pauses add up to 20 seconds of waiting on the confirmation page, in addition to time spent
+calling the gateway. If the final attempt times out, the timeout is raised to the caller.
+
+During the gateway's Friday 17:00–19:00 peak, the previous three attempts went out within a second and all hit the
+same slow period. One Friday left 58 confirmed pantry orders for a volunteer to capture by hand the next morning.
+A sandbox replay with the longer retry schedule would have captured 57 of those 58 orders. The team accepted the
+added wait to reduce that manual work; switching gateways was deferred because the contract runs through December
+2026. [Issue 40](../../notes/issue-40.md) records the discussion and replay result.
 
